A||||31||FieroKyle||Why GM is so great......||||7||
Z||000000||FieroKyle||10-26-2001||11:28 PM||||Alright, have noticed some hatred for GM lately with there recent lineup that has included the ass-tek (cough.... I mean aztek)and Avalanche. And above all the cancelation of Fieros, Camaros, and the TransAm/FireBird. To add to that the recent cancelation in clutch pedals notified from Archie. LoL<P>Heres the deal, well in my eyes anyways. Probably might get some short tempers and flaming for it, but hopefully you guys have cool heads and will promise not to "shoot cops" and pull out a "butterfly knife", cough cough......  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The Aztek is a pretty good performer for what it is. Once you climb into the cockpit, you really can't see the ugly outside, but notice people do give long stares of the question "why???". But it has a lot of uses in the end for the good.<P>The Avalanche I actually sorta like. If ya get the higher hoursepower (I think its 275 or 325???) It ought to be a really great performer. It can go through pretty much anything and still hauls stuff pretty decent.<P>Chevy's truck line up is great, there is something for everyone including its diesel with like 500 to 600 lbs of torque. nuff said. GM is also coming out with the SSR with the LS1 engine. Outta keep right up with the ford lighting and personally I like the looks of it from what I have seen. Sorta like a truck roadster from the 50's deal. Pretty neat stuff.<P>Monte Carlo I think is a great looking car and a pretty decent performer. In NASCAR, the only thing that has it beat on the street is the Grand Prix GTP which is made by GM also.<P>Pontiac's line up include the GTP and the Bonneville SSEI, great cars, great performers. Then the sporty commuter sunfire which isn't a bad car either.<P>Oldsmobile has the Aurora for its gem, and with the V-8, those suckers haul. Then it has the Intrigue and Silhouette and so on. All good cars in my opinion.<P>Caddys - luxury liners with the N*, all great cars if ya like the huge price tag. The Escalade, that is one bad ass SUV, fast, luxurious, and so on. I love em. They blow the Navigator away.<P>Buick, well just granny cars except they are gonna produce the Bengal with the 3800 II supercharged in them. Should be a pretty cool car.<P>As for the TransAm/Camaro, its sad. I will miss them, but GM will replace them down the road. They won't stand the Mustang as the only muscle car type competition which GM has blown them away at in recent years.<P>There are many other great cars that I forgot to mention, like the new Trailblazer/Envoy. You guys can add on to this or do whatever. Probably give me all these numbers why Ford is better or Dodge, I don't care (speeds, crash tests, blah blah, I think GM has most of those covered anyway)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I am just saying GM I think by far is the best automaker. Just my 2 cents and then some more.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||7
