Z||000003||BlackStang95||10-27-2001||12:00 AM||||Seriously kyle, brand loyalty is one thing, stupidity is another.  You think I like focuses or escorts or anything? hell no.  The navigators are more luxorious and look better than the escalade (whats up with the 12 inch caddy symbol?) and people dont buy suvs for speed.  The asstek and avalanche speak for themselves, ive never seen anyone defend them before.  The f-body was getting outsold by the Mustang to the tune of 100,000 units or something like that, and looked to be totally blown away after the mustangs re-design.  Just the facts man.<P>Oh...and the ssr?  I don't like the looks, but they get 0-60 in an estimated 7 seconds (motortrend).  Good lunk hunting a lightning with that.  Not to mention a 4 foot bed thats covered all the time is not much of a truck.  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierozilla||10-27-2001||12:03 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  The Aztec is ugly, period.<BR>The Bonneville is ok, but nothing special. At least nothing I'd ever buy.<BR>The Olds Aurora?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>Buick has the Rendesvous (spell?) and thats pretty cool for yet another SUV I guess.<BR>The Monte Carlo is just plain a$$ UGLY.<BR>The Avalanche and other Chevy trucks are pretty nice.<BR>Cadillacs are garbage, NEVER would I pay that much for an American luxury car. <BR>Ive NEVER seen a "non gang-banger" drive an Escalade either.<BR>You didnt mention the Vette...they're sweet, no doubt, but WAY over priced.<BR>I'm about at my witts end w/ GM. Next NEW car wont be a GM product, that much is certain.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Fierozilla (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroKyle||10-27-2001||12:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>BS95, how lame can you be?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Exactly....<BR>I was talking performance numbers about the stangs vs f-bodies. V-8 stang vs V-8 f-body, or v-6 stang vs v-6 f-bodies...... WHAT AM I DOING!!!!! I AM REVIVING THIS STUPID FIGHT AGAIN, NOOOOOO!!!!! IT MUST STOP!!!!! Uh, for you lately, probably it isn't your best interest to be posting stuff like that cuz one thing seems to lead to another with you.<P>I defended the asstek as a car, not a totally fashionable vechile to be driving in. What did you say???? Navigator so much better than Escalade???? Your full of  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">. Cadilac paid so much attention to fine detail in it and it really comes together as a great vehcile. I know many people have not agreed with the exterior of some of GM's new models, but overall they are great. And if I am paying the much for an SUV, it better be a great performer. Escalade can beat most of the V-8 Mustangs Mr. 0-60 expert. NO I AM STARTING THE FIGHT AGAIN!!! PLEASE MAKE ME STOP!!! I AM HAVING SUCH A HARD TIME NOT DOING SOMETHING RASH TO THIS GUY! Well anyways. <P>Kyle 85' GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroKyle||10-27-2001||12:13 AM||||The chevy Corvette Z-06, 50k for a Super car that has 405 hp and does 0-60 just under 4 secs??? Uh I don't think so. Since the Porshes and Ferraris that run similar numbers, but still get blown away cost 80k or more. Well, I like most of GMs new cars. I told ya, its my opinion.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Spektrum-87GT||10-27-2001||12:25 AM||||i respect your opinion. Although I dont agree with a lot of it. you mentioned nascar... just so you know in the future, the monte carlo they use in racing uses like negative 2 parts off the one they sell at dealerships. i do agreee that the gtp and bonneville are great looking cars, with great engines to boot. The avalanche is a joke rip off in my opinion, along with every other suv/truck gm makes(OPINION). Oldsmobile is dead. My friends dad has a buick regal thats a little over a year old. It's already been to the shop many times and is rattling. In my opinion, gm hasnt been a good car company since the 60s. Stupid decisions by executives *COUGH*fiero*COUGH*, following trends, and creating inferior cars is why I hate gm. think about it, what has gm done during its lifetime as a company. Cancel their sports cars. Do you know why? They dont sell. Why is that? i dont know, but the mustang doesnt have any problem. I'm not pro ford by a long shot. I dont hate them like I hate gm though. You know the main reason I hate gm? the 89 fiero. It was an animal, a straight beast of a car. The ones that were created were all crushed(at least one still exists in some pontiac parking lot, somewhere) and the car was never released. Why? some stupid gm executive(that idiot president) cancelled them due to 'lack of sales'. Personally, I dont believe it. Why would gm sink so much money into developing a car like the 89 fiero just to scrap it? Pontiac has always been the red headed step child of gm, while chevy has been the generic pretty boy that is pampered. The 89 fiero was faster than the 89 corvette, looked better, and was cheaper(according to reporters). This is why the 89 fiero never came out. gm sucks, and they probably always will suck. GM's name should be changed to GCAM... generic crap ass motors.<P>Before you flame. This has been my opinion. I respect your opinion, so please respect mine.||||reg||1
Z||000008||BlackStang95||10-27-2001||12:31 AM||||Wow...looks like I gotta correct kyle on his numbers again. <P>escalade gets mid 7's 0-60.  That will run with v6 stangs, not v-8's, and for 50k they should.<P>corvette z06?  you were wayyyy off.  385 hp, 0-60 in 4.8, 1/4 of 13.1.  Yes 50k is a bit high for that.  Don't believe me?  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.edmunds.com/reviews/roadtests/roadtest/43875/page002.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.edmunds.com/reviews/roadtests/roadtest/43875/page002.html</A> <P>What else you got?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Nashco||10-27-2001||12:32 AM||||In general, I don't see any of those cars jumping out at me as fantastic.  <P>I think the Escalade would make a good pulling rig(have you seen the options for it?)...if you want an overpriced pulling rig.  <P>I think the new monte looks ugly, and deserves more power.  <P>I like the Aztek (go ahead...flame me, I don't give a flying frick), and it is very versatile; I'll be interested to see how well they hold up though.  <P>Personally, I think the SSR looks uglier than any truck ever made...BUT, it is supposed to share the same drivetrain as the new S series, and I'd love to see factory v8 blazers and trucks, as they have been prominent in the aftermarker forever.<P>Avalance doesn't rank high in my looks department, but I think the back of the cab is interesting.<P>GTP and SSEI, great deal for those who like people in their car and still good power.  I'd much rather have the Aurora though...they're damn quick.<P>Buick...if the Bengal is supposed to be anything like their show car last year, I'd be surprised to EVER see it on the road.  It was way too cool; if it ever does make it, it'll be the uncoolified version.<P>TransAm/Camaro....as if there aren't enough of them out there.  I view this as a good thing; it will suck the REAL performance buyers to the surface, and create demand for a REAL sports car!  I don't know, there are waaay too many secondary, tertiary, etc, side effects...only time will tell.<P>There are some things that people just look past.  Take a cavalier, for example...mostly cheap stuff, but have you driven a new 5 speed?  It shifts as smooth as any tranny I've ever used, and has a reverse lockout built into the shifter.  I was thoroughly impressed.<P>I'm more of a European car fan; the<BR>engineering in those cars is far superior, as is the manufacturing to American cars.  I feel their manufacturing is equivalent to Japanese, but the designs make them better.  All opinion, no hard evidence.<P>Don't forget to mention the Corvette, which is getting better every year...keep on it Chevy.  I would choose a Viper over it any day, but to each his own.<P>Ok, my 2.9 cents...<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jaei Sun||10-27-2001||12:41 AM||||GM said they cancelled the fiero because the sales of two seaters is dismal.  SO what do they do the next year?? Release the BUICK REATTA.  That blows that excuse away.  And it only lasted for a 3-4 years.  Meanwhile MAZDA has been selling the Miata for 10+ years without a problem.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Rick 88||10-27-2001||12:55 AM||||I had heard the 3.5 24 valve Shortstar was going to be the replacement for the 3800 pushrod engines. The 3.5 would make a nice Fiero swap as well.<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
Z||000012||Flamberge||10-27-2001||03:56 AM||||I like the Buick Reatta. After the Fiero it is one of the best looking of GM's cars... (Though a close up of its cockpit gives away its Buick-ness.) <P>I like(d) the Firebird 4th Gen. I think the 1998+ Formula is the best looking production car for any company...ever. There I said it. My opinion of course, but to me they got everything right, styling-wise. But now it is dead.<P>The Bonney looks better than it did, but still needs work. The Grand Am is getting a bit abstract too. The Grand Prix motors on though, a car that might be in my (future) garage one of these days. The Sunfire 2 door is okay, but the "restyled" front end sucks compared to when it first came out, and they both suck compared to the show car version of the Sunfire. Having a minivan in the Pontiac line up is the perfect metaphor for why GM is hurting.<P>Chevrolet - yes the 'vette is nice, and overpriced. The Cavalier is okay.<P>Buick - My mom is a Buick freak, but I think the only recent Buick worth its wheels was the 87 Regal Grand National. This is the GM Division that should have died first.<P>Olds - Just beginning to figure things out. The Aurora, though overweight and ugly, has a nice engine. The Intrique is very nice styling-wise, well proportioned. The Alero has HUGE taillights! Dang.<P>Caddy - They should make only 2 models, a very nice top end luxury car, to compete with Lexus, Acura, BMW, etc, and a fast exotic. The Cien is a step in the right direction there.<P>Saturn - Don't become completely assimilated by the company that made you, or you will drown in its mediocrity!<P>My $21,565.02<P><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||AusFiero||10-27-2001||05:48 AM||||Ok from an Australian perspective I only have one GM car to mention. Commodore HSV GTS. 400hp 5.7 ltr, 6 speed gearbox, 4 doors and a full size boot/trunk. Beats all its compretition inluding M3 beemers and most euro cars. <BR>What more could a GM lover want  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000014||lou||10-27-2001||06:21 AM||||GM has long lost its edge.  The innovation and energy that created the Fiero has been completely eradicated.  Now they are concentrating on their high dollar vehicles.  This is why the Firebird is no longer being made, once again Chevrolet dictates the demise of its own sibling. Simple formula; pay more and you get more technology.  How many vehicles can you sell over $40,000 ? Especially when they last longer and are more reliable than the vehicles made 10 years ago.  Gm is the largest corporation in the world, however they are out of touch with their most important market.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Formula||10-27-2001||07:06 AM||||Blackstang: the ZO6 was bumped up to 405hp for the next model year.  And I agree that an escalade couldn't run with a Stang GT, I doubt that it could seriously run with a V6 stang either.<P>Cavalier is, in my opinion, the new escort.  You see everyone driving them and they are cheap and in every salvage yard.  They are more of an escort then the focus or zx2 anyway.  ford ended up overpricing the escort compared to the 80s and lost its niche.<P>Corvettes are still the most affordable supercar on the planet.  If I could afford a top of the line car like that I would buy a viper though.<P>Chevy Extreme S-10, Excellent styling for gen X.  Now that they are getting 4.3 L V6s they are a kicka$$ truck!  The new SSR  is  basically a V8 extreme, with a really short bed.  Both killer ideas.<P>Camaro/Firebird, they lost the pony car wars to the mustang, not because of of HP or Handling, but because they are oversized, overpriced, sport luxury (GT) cars.  They need a shorter wheelbase, smaller (cheaper) motor and boxier (Pony Car) look to them.  The f-bodies are more of an original muscle car (bigger) then a pony car (what they are).  The mustang is still a pony car and a great one at that. <P><BR>Nothing else stands out too much to me for the General.<p>[This message has been edited by Formula (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fformula88||10-27-2001||12:10 PM||||Looks like a lot of consessions to owning a GM.  I mean, the Aztek is a good performer and you cannot see its bad exterior when driving it?  For my $20-$30K on a new car, all those concessions should not be necessary.  Period.||||reg||1
Z||000017||BlackStang95||10-27-2001||12:14 PM||||Ah, 20 hp is a nice boost.  But I dont see it making it a full second faster 0-60 (as kyle claimed).  Don't get me wrong, i'd nearly sell my soul for a new z06   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   i just think they are still overpriced because they are about a second faster than gt's and about double the price. <P>For 2001 the z06 got 13.1, the mustang cobra got 13.8.  50k vs 30k.  Easy decision I think.<P>just my thoughts<p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||sqoach||10-27-2001||12:24 PM||||Um...I'll just stick with my Fiero for now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">              <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Jake_Dragon||10-27-2001||12:40 PM||||Enjoy your ride, when its over get in another line. I have never owned a new car, I like my rides tested. Every car I have owned I have drove till I found something else that catches my eye. Besides the Fiero, the Dodge Charger is the only car I have had 2 at once. I have owned several Chevy and one Ford. I have even found myself looking at imports lately. Don't close your mind because its not GM.<P>Given the time and money I would be driving this:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.rodster.com/images/Sdred1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||FieroKyle||10-27-2001||08:52 PM||||Is it this coming year, the Vette people decided to add 20 more hp to the z06. The Monte SS is a bit faster than the LS, not a ton, but noticable by far.<P>Here is the Vette information straight from GM. <A HREF="http://www.chevrolet.com/corvette/index_z06.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.chevrolet.com/corvette/index_z06.htm</A> <P>The Vette is gonna have to be getting pumped for its 50th anverisary edition coming up, the Viper is trying to spoil the party with its new model in 2003.<P>The vette by far is a better performer than the Mustang. May be the Trans Am with the LS1 is a bit better competition for ya.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
