Z||000022||Nashco||10-27-2001||09:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>Chevy Extreme S-10, Excellent styling for gen X.  Now that they are getting 4.3 L V6s they are a kicka$$ truck!  The new SSR  is  basically a V8 extreme, with a really short bed.  Both killer ideas.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>FYI, the S-10 has had the 4.3 for a very long time, and they have always been quick for a truck.  The 4.3 Xtreme nowadays doesn't hold a candle to the turbo'd Syclone/Typhoon in my opinion.  The S series aren't just getting sporty now...they have been.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000023||firstfiero||10-27-2001||11:12 PM||||     Just saw the new vette on motor trend televison the other night. 20 more horsies. That should take about .5 off the 0 to 60 time. The Lightning lost .5 from it's time with addition of 20 hp. I think it's about 5.2 now and it was about 5.7. Damn I love that truck. <BR>     I like the avalanche! But then I have a Ford Explorer Sportrack. Alot of my friends find that really ugly. My Mustang friends think it's crazy to pay 32 grand for that when I could of had a mustang cobra for actually less. What I hate is gm's usual crap of putting a cadilac emblem on the avalanche and adding 10 grand. They'll never get that that crap doesn't work.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
