Z||000025||Pontiaddict||10-28-2001||02:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>By far?  By 7 tenths of a second and 20 grand.  My numbers were from a neutral 3rd party.  20 hp does not equal half a second, especially when you already have 385.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It may have been a neutral 3rd party, but it's a neutral 3rd party that doesn't know how to drive a Corvette.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>From the Edmunds.com website:<BR><B>This car just explodes off the line. Talk about torque! There is nothing but tire spin if you launch over 2,000 rpms with traction control turned off. I aborted two runs because I launched with massive tire spin. The best runs were with the traction control off and a solid low rpm launch. Launch technique was critical with this car, and with a little more practice, we think we could have gotten quarter-mile times under 13 seconds.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not that there needs to be a pro driver for every test, but from reading other articles off that website, I don't think that testing accuraccy is high on their list of proirities.||||reg||1
