Z||000031||Sophia Nova||10-28-2001||03:22 PM||||I live in Lansing, MI, so I'm very biased toward GMs.  I have owned GMs all my life (all 19 years of it) excluding a passed-down Ford Crown Victoria, and I have to say GM really has lost its edge and it is sad.  Cancelling the Camaro and Firebird are, in my opinion, big mistakes.  Those are great cars and always will be the epitome of the legendary muscle cars.  I cannot stand the way the Aztek looks although it did receive some good reviews.  And that one truck you all are talking about is way ugly, too.  I'm only commenting on looks, however.  Performance may be an entirely different story.   GM had its heyday last millenium but they still put out great, reliable cars albeit they may not be the best-looking or best-performing car on the market.  <BR>Sophia Nova<P>||||reg||1
